    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.04-07",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Allocation can be proportionate to group size or deliberately equal for a comparison, but the choice affects interpretation. If a population is 80% residents and 20% visitors, a sample of ten from each gives equal groups that are good for comparing, but it does not show how many of each type of person live there. State which design was used. Do not silently treat equal group counts as the actual population mix.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-4.1.04-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.04-2",
        "CL-6137-4.1.04-01-1",
        "CL-6137-4.1.04-01-2",
