    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.04-08",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The methods can combine. A stratified random design first defines zones and then randomly chooses eligible sites in each. A stratified systematic design can use a regular rule within each zone. This is not a contradiction: the terms describe different stages. Explain both the group coverage and within-group selection rather than assign a complicated label without an operating sequence.",
