      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A teaching diagram can show a safe grid with numbered eligible stations, a regular transect and two shaded habitat zones. Random selection marks a stated random draw; systematic selection marks a stated interval; stratified selection includes sites from each defined zone. Site symbols, boundaries and eligibility must remain clear.\n\n![Sampling diagram: random, systematic and stratified selection in one area](../../assets/images/ITEM-6137-4.1-021-PROC-answer.png)",
