    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.04-10",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "No design removes every bias. Refusals, inaccessible sites, measurement problems, time coverage and an incomplete frame can still affect results. A good evaluation identifies which part is limited and suggests a matched change. Saying “use random sampling” does not solve a badly worded questionnaire, and a larger sample does not calibrate an instrument. Choose the improvement that addresses the actual weakness.",
