    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.04-11",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A sample frame can be spatial or social. A numbered grid represents eligible positions; a list represents eligible people or premises; a timetable represents possible observation periods. The random mechanism operates within that frame. If important positions or groups are absent, random selection from the incomplete list does not restore them. Coverage should therefore be assessed before drawing numbers.",
