    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.04-12",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A systematic pedestrian sample might use every fifth eligible passer-by after a stated start. The investigator must define who is eligible and avoid resetting the sequence whenever a person looks unwilling or inconvenient. Participation still remains voluntary: refusals are recorded according to the planned rule. This distinguishes selection from consent and prevents a systematic label concealing convenience replacement.",
