    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.04-13",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A stratified tourism comparison can select twenty resident respondents and twenty visitors to compare the groups. If twelve residents and sixteen visitors answer positively under the same neutral item, the sample proportions are 60% and 80%. Equal sample sizes make that comparison clear, but do not show that the wider population contains equal numbers of residents and visitors. A figure for the whole population needs the real number of residents and visitors. Equal groups suit this survey because its aim is to compare how residents and visitors answered.",
