      "block_id": "BL-6137-4.1.04-14",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The proportionate alternative allocates sample size using known group shares where feasible. If the eligible population has eighty residents and twenty visitors, a proportionate sample of twenty would include sixteen and four under that design. The smaller visitor sample may be less useful for a detailed group comparison. The choice depends on the enquiry objective, which should be stated rather than treating equal or proportionate allocation as universally superior.",
